---
name: orchestrator
description: 'Multi-stage pipeline orchestration using 3 executables (ppt_analyze → photon_tracer → ppt_diagnose). Use when: wiring the analyze→render→diagnose pipeline, setting up preview or production rendering, coordinating skill invocation order, configuring render parameters, or debugging stage-to-stage data flow.'
---

# Orchestrator

Meta-skill that coordinates the rendering pipeline across 3 executables. Owns no source files — determines **which tools to invoke, in what order, with what config, and how to verify**.

## 3-Executable Pipeline

```
ppt_analyze scene.pbrt           → stdout: profile.json (scene metrics + recommended config)
    ↓
photon_tracer --config profile.json scene.pbrt → output.exr + render_log.json
    ↓
ppt_diagnose output.exr render_log.json → stdout: report.json (artifacts + corrections)
```

### Feedback Loop

```
for iteration in 1..3:
    profile = ppt_analyze(scene)
    render(scene, profile)
    report = ppt_diagnose(output)
    if report.artifacts.empty(): break
    apply report.corrections to profile
```

### Data Flow

| Producer | Output | Consumer |
|----------|--------|----------|
| `ppt_analyze` | `profile.json` (SceneProfile + RenderConfig) | `photon_tracer` (via --config) |
| `photon_tracer` | `output.exr` + `render_log.json` | `ppt_diagnose` |
| `ppt_diagnose` | `report.json` (artifacts + corrections) | orchestrator (feedback) |

## Skills → Executables

| Skill | Executable | Invocation |
|-------|-----------|------------|
| **scene-analysis** | `ppt_analyze` | `ppt_analyze <scene>` |
| **renderer** | `photon_tracer` | `photon_tracer [--config X] <scene>` |
| **post-processing** | `photon_tracer` | Built into renderer; params via config |
| **quality** | `ppt_diagnose` | `ppt_diagnose <output.exr> [render_log.json]` |
| **test-harness** | `ppt_tests` | Test runner |
| **scene-editor** | `scene_editor` | `scene_editor <scene>` |

## Config Override Cascade

CLI args > JSON config (`--config`) > SceneProfile auto-tune > compile-time defaults (`config.h`)

## CLI Reference

All flags supported by `photon_tracer`:

| Flag | Type | Default | Controls |
|------|------|---------|----------|
| `--config FILE` | string | — | Load JSON config |
| `--save-config FILE` | string | — | Save current config to JSON |
| `--width N` | int | 768 | Image width |
| `--height N` | int | 768 | Image height |
| `--spp N` | int | 256 | Samples per pixel |
| `--bounces N` | int | 8 | Max camera bounces |
| `--photons N` | int | 2M | Global photon budget |
| `--caustic-photons N` | int | 2M | Caustic photon budget |
| `--exposure F` | float | 1.0 | Tone map exposure |
| `--light-scale F` | float | 1.0 | Light intensity multiplier (combined with exposure) |
| `--output FILE` | string | output/render.png | Output PNG path |
| `--guide-fraction F` | float | 0.5 | Guided sampling fraction |
| `--no-guide` | flag | — | Disable guided path tracing |
| `--no-denoiser` | flag | — | Disable OptiX AI denoiser |
| `--no-aces` | flag | — | Disable ACES tonemapping |
| `--no-bloom` | flag | — | Disable bloom post-FX |
| `--no-firefly` | flag | — | Disable firefly filter |
| `--no-path-clamp` | flag | — | Disable per-path throughput clamping (sets limit to 1e30) |
| `--mode MODE` | string | full | full\|direct\|indirect\|photon\|normals\|material\|depth\|guide |
| `--gather-radius F` | float | 0.05 | Max photon gather radius |
| `--knn-k N` | int | 100 | k-NN neighbors |
| `--adaptive` | flag | — | Enable adaptive sampling |
| `--rr-threshold F` | float | 0.95 | Russian roulette threshold |
| `--max-sample-luminance F` | float | 10000 | Per-sample luminance clamp |
| `--nee-light-samples N` | int | 4 | NEE light samples per hit |
| `--sweep [SPP,...]` | int list | 16,64,256,512,1024,2048 | Convergence sweep (implies --headless) |
| `--headless` | flag | — | No window (batch render + save) |

All 60 `RenderConfig` fields can also be set via `--config` JSON files. See `src/renderer/app/render_config_json.cpp` for the full list.
